=== first attempt, kept with its refutation ===
clamp_top_only_unconstrained_floor: one clamp (ceiling), operands of both signs
  top=3   operands in [  -7,7   ] triples=   3375  assoc-failures=904   H1 predicted 0, got this
  top=8   operands in [ -12,12  ] triples=  15625  assoc-failures=3244   H1 predicted 0, got this
  top=15  operands in [ -19,19  ] triples=  59319  assoc-failures=10468   H1 predicted 0, got this

=== second attempt, the discriminating case ===
non-negative operands (0..=N), one clamp at the top, floor never reached:
  top=3   operands in [0,12 ] triples=   2197  assoc-failures=0
  top=8   operands in [0,16 ] triples=   4913  assoc-failures=0
  top=15  operands in [0,24 ] triples=  15625  assoc-failures=0

non-negative operands (0..=N), TWO clamps (explicit floor 0, ceiling top),
floor still structurally unreachable from non-negative operands:
  lo=0 hi=3   operands in [0,12 ] triples=   2197  assoc-failures=0
  lo=0 hi=8   operands in [0,16 ] triples=   4913  assoc-failures=0
  lo=0 hi=15  operands in [0,24 ] triples=  15625  assoc-failures=0

non-negative operands (0..=N), TWO clamps where the floor IS reachable
(a positive floor above 0, so a small enough partial sum clamps low):
  lo=2   hi=10  operands in [0,14 ] triples=   3375  assoc-failures=48
  lo=5   hi=20  operands in [0,26 ] triples=  19683  assoc-failures=450

H1 (one clamp associates, two do not) predicts failures in the second and third
blocks above and none in the first. H2 (confinement to a half-line that already
contains the result associates, regardless of clamp count) predicts failures
only in the fourth block, where the floor is actually reachable, and none in the
second or third.
